<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- NOT sandboxed, deliberately. NightMail is Developer ID signed and
	     notarized and ships outside the Mac App Store, so the sandbox is
	     optional — and the in-app updater cannot work inside one:

	     * `desktop_updater` verifies a staged app by spawning `spctl` and
	       `xcrun stapler`. Children inherit the sandbox: `spctl` answers
	       "internal error in Code Signing subsystem" and `xcrun` refuses
	       outright ("cannot be used within an App Sandbox"). No entitlement
	       fixes either — xcrun's refusal is its own check, not the kernel's.
	     * The install handoff registers a privileged helper through
	       `SMAppService.daemon`, which a sandboxed app may not do.

	     `../inkworm`, which this updater was modelled on, and desktop_updater's
	     own example app both ship unsandboxed for the same reason.

	     Consequences that used to be handled by entitlements here:
	     * network.client / network.server are unnecessary — the Gmail OAuth
	       loopback bind (LoopbackAuthFlow, 127.0.0.1:34572) needs no
	       permission outside the sandbox.
	     * files.user-selected.read-write is unnecessary.
	     * personal-information.addressbook / .calendars must NOT be here.
	       They are sandbox-only entitlements, and on a non-sandboxed build
	       they make CNContactStore return authorizationDenied without ever
	       showing a dialog — see macOS Privacy Permissions in CLAUDE.md.
	       Contacts and Calendar access come from the Info.plist usage
	       strings instead.

	     keychain-access-groups stays. Every account, OAuth token and IMAP
	     password lives in the Keychain under this group, and the group is what
	     keeps them readable across this change — dropping it would sign the
	     user out of everything. It is why the release build still needs the
	     Developer ID provisioning profile the workflow embeds. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<false/>
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)au.com.sharpblue.nightmail</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
